# Deck 🖼️

facet agent

Type a topic; it writes a slide deck and renders it as a live **reveal.js** presentation you can
present right there (arrow keys, `f` for fullscreen). An example of pulling in a real front-end
dependency — `reveal.js` from a CDN — and building the slide components in a `.work` `client` block,
fed by a `server` block that generates the outline with `Nexus.Llm`.

## Adding a dependency

The interface block loads `reveal.js` (+ a theme) straight off a CDN and builds each slide as a
`<section>` — so "I'm adding reveal.js and authoring my slides with it" is just a `client` block. The
deck content comes from the `server` block below; the data model is a `Deck` row.

resource Presentation do
  topic :text
  title :text
  slides :int
end

## The deck writer

`run/2` asks the model for a structured outline (a JSON array of slides), then streams each slide to
the interface as it's parsed, so the deck builds in front of you.

server :deck do
  @model "google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it"

  def register do
    Nexus.Live.register("deck", fn params, emit ->
      topic = params["q"] || ""
      result = run(topic, emit)

      try do
        Nexus.Store.create(Presentation, %{topic: topic, title: result.title, slides: length(result.slides)})
      rescue
        _ -> :ok
      end
    end)
  end

  def run(topic, emit) do
    emit.(%{type: "step", label: "Outlining “#{topic}”…"})
    slides = generate(topic)

    Enum.each(slides, fn s -> emit.(%{type: "slide", slide: s}) end)

    title = (List.first(slides) || %{title: topic})[:title] || topic
    emit.(%{type: "done", title: title})
    %{topic: topic, title: title, slides: slides}
  rescue
    _ ->
      emit.(%{type: "done", title: topic})
      %{topic: topic, title: topic, slides: []}
  end

  defp generate(topic) do
    prompt =
      "Write a clear, well-structured slide deck on: #{topic}\n\n" <>
        "Return ONLY a JSON array of 6-9 slides, each an object: " <>
        "{\"title\": string, \"bullets\": [string], \"notes\": string}. " <>
        "The FIRST slide is a title slide (one or two bullets as a subtitle). Content slides have " <>
        "3-5 SHORT bullets. `notes` is a one-line speaker note. No markdown, no prose outside the JSON."

    case Nexus.Llm.complete([%{role: "user", content: prompt}], model: @model, max_tokens: 1800) do
      {:ok, %{content: c}} when is_binary(c) and c != "" -> parse(c)
      _ -> []
    end
  end

  # Pull the JSON array out of the response and normalize each slide. Degrades to [] on a bad shape.
  defp parse(c) do
    json =
      case Regex.run(~r/\[.*\]/s, c) do
        [m] -> m
        _ -> c
      end

    case Jason.decode(json) do
      {:ok, list} when is_list(list) -> list |> Enum.map(&slide/1) |> Enum.reject(&is_nil/1)
      _ -> []
    end
  end

  defp slide(%{} = s) do
    %{
      title: text(s["title"]),
      bullets: (s["bullets"] || []) |> List.wrap() |> Enum.map(&text/1) |> Enum.reject(&(&1 == "")),
      notes: text(s["notes"])
    }
  end

  defp slide(_), do: nil

  defp text(v) when is_binary(v), do: String.trim(v)
  defp text(_), do: ""
end
